    "result_text": "Both tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented \"mark an invoice as paid, with a record kept\" as a small full-stack, additive change:\n\n**Database** \u2014 `V5__invoice_status.sql`: new migration adding a `status VARCHAR(16) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'UNPAID'` column to `invoice` (additive, defaulted, existing rows unaffected).\n\n**Server (OfficeFloor + Spring)**\n- `Invoice.java` \u2014 added the `status` field with getter/setter.\n- `InvoicePay.java` + `PayInvoice.java` + `rest/api/invoices/pay.POST.yml` \u2014 a new endpoint `POST /api/invoices/pay` that loads the invoice, flips it to `PAID`, saves, and audits via the `Audit` service with the exact record the test expects: `INVOICE_PAID id=1 amount=100.00`.\n- `InvoicesPost.java` \u2014 sets `status=\"UNPAID\"` on create so new invoices start unpaid (JPA would otherwise insert NULL and bypass the DB default).\n- `TestSupportController.java` \u2014 seed now inserts the `status` column (defaulting to `UNPAID` when the fixture omits it).\n\n**Front-end** \u2014 extended the invoices feature's own `InvoicesPanel.tsx`: added a `status` field to the `Invoice` type, a `data-testid=\"invoice-status\"` cell, and a `data-testid=\"invoice-pay-<id>\"` button wired to a `useMutation` that POSTs to `/api/invoices/pay` and invalidates the `['invoices']` query key so the row re-renders as `PAID`.\n\nVerification: `npm run typecheck` passes and `bin/e2e` shows both spec tests green (status flips UNPAID\u2192PAID in the UI, and the audit record is written).",
